 ### NeRF Network Architecture with Blend Weight Field
 This architecture extends the radiance field with a blend weight field $F_{\Delta w}$ to handle dynamic human bodies [S6].
-**Parameters:** Sampling uses single-level NeRF with 64 points along each camera ray. Appearance code and blend weight field code dimensions are both 128 [S6].
-**Network Layout:** Radiance fields $F_\sigma, F_c$ follow the original NeRF architecture. Blend weight field $F_{\Delta w}$ is almost identical to $F_\sigma$, except the final output layer has 24 channels and applies $\exp(\cdot)$ to the output [S6].
-**Steps:** Train parameters of $F_\sigma, F_c, F_{\Delta w}$, appearance codes $\{\mathbf{l}_i\}$ and blend weight field codes $\{\boldsymbol{\psi}_i\}$ jointly over the input video. Learn neural blend weight fields under novel human poses using equation (9) from the source. Use Adam optimizer with learning rate starting from $5 \times 10^{-4}$ decaying exponentially to $5 \times 10^{-5}$ [S6].
