 ## Background
-Neural Radiance Fields (NeRF) were introduced by Mildenhall et al. in 2020, establishing the baseline continuous volumetric representation [G]. Subsequent research has modified this architecture to handle specific challenges such as dynamic scenes [S5], noise [S1], semantic understanding [S1], and efficient inference [S2]. The modifications described here represent the evolution of the NeRF architecture from a static, monolithic MLP to specialized, multi-component systems.
